# Time-boxed acceptances only — every entry needs a reason and an expiry.

# OpenSSL unbounded memory growth in QUIC (libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2).
# Debian shipped the fix (3.5.7-1~deb13u2) but gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian13
# has not rebuilt on it yet (digest checked 2026-08-26). Node links its own
# OpenSSL statically and the server does not speak QUIC, so the vulnerable
# shared lib is not on any request path. Re-check the base digest before expiry.
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-09-30

# zstd information disclosure via uninitialized memory (libzstd1 1.5.7+dfsg-1).
# Debian shipped the fix (1.5.7+dfsg-1+deb13u1) but gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian13
# has not rebuilt on it yet (latest digest sha256:39b04073… checked 2026-11-25 with
# Trivy 0.69.1: same finding). The Debian libzstd1 is not loaded by the server: the API
# process's /proc/1/maps on Chronos dev (2026-11-25, image 3d1272d4) maps no zstd library.
# Node bundles its own zstd 1.5.7, and the server never compresses responses with zstd;
# request bodies in zstd are refused with 415 since 335e6537 (requestEncodings in
# registerCompression), so no request reaches a zstd decoder. Re-check the base digest
# before expiry and bump it (as in 29e1c25c) once it carries deb13u1.
CVE-2026-124851 exp:2026-12-09
